<a> DaveD mentioned schedctl on Solaris lets you find out if a thread is currently blocked. So
    from lock find owner and see if its not running then dont spin just park!!

    Not sure if it uses a system call for this and/or how fast it is. My idea was to have 
    user mode register a piece of code with kernel at the start and optionally with a flag
    ask OS to invoke it out its switch_out. The OS can ignore it if it chooses btw.

    When we acquire a lock we set a bit that says run X on switch out. On lock release reset
    this bit. 

    The code X essentially sets a flag in the lock struct saying lock owner is not currently
    running do not spin. 

    If we added switch_in hook then when lock owner gets sliced in it could set the flag to false 
    again.


<b> My idea to prevent spinning beyond one timeslice is as follows:

    --> Pure SW solution:
    	Use the on_switch_out to park if spinning doesnt succeed.


